Ingredients:

   - 10 ounces skinless, boneless chicken breasts, cut into thin strips
   - =C2=BD onion, cut into strips
   - 5 ounces multi-colored bell pepper strips
   - 2 tablespoons vegetable oil
   - =C2=BD lime, juiced
   - 2 tablespoons fajita seasoning
   - 4 (12 inch) flour tortillas
   - 1 cup refried beans, warmed
   - =E2=85=94 cup shredded Cheddar cheese
   - 1 =C2=BD cups cooked Mexican rice
   - =C2=BC cup sour cream
   - =E2=85=93 cup guacamole

Instructions:

   1. *Marinate the Chicken*: Place the chicken, onion, bell pepper, oil,
   lime juice, and fajita seasoning in a resealable plastic bag. Seal the b=
ag
   and squeeze to ensure all ingredients are combined and well-coated.
   Marinate in the refrigerator for 2 hours.
   2. *Cook the Fajita Mixture*: Preheat the oven to 400=C2=B0F (200=C2=B0C=
). Line a
   sheet pan with foil. Spread the fajita mixture onto the sheet pan in a
   single layer. Bake until the chicken juices run clear, about 25 minutes.=
 An
   instant-read thermometer inserted into the chicken strips should read 16=
5=C2=B0F
   (74=C2=B0C).
   3. *Warm the Tortillas*: Wrap the tortillas in a damp paper towel and
   warm in the microwave until soft and pliable, about 30 seconds.
   4. *Assemble the Burritos*: Spread =C2=BC of the refried beans, cheese, =
rice,
   fajita mixture, sour cream, and guacamole in a line across the middle of
   each tortilla. Fold the sides of the tortilla in, overlapping the fillin=
g.
   Roll the bottom edge up tightly around the filling, then roll the burrit=
o
   away from you, keeping the sides folded in.

